{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1216214,"duration_api_ms":1209190,"num_turns":102,"result":"Everything looks correct. Now I'll produce the final ExecutionPayload JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Validate nitrification-driven alkalinity depletion with the carbonate solver, expose diagnostics, and prepare the denitrification return path. Added named stoichiometric constants NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N (2/14.007 ≈ 0.1428 meq/mg N) and DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N (1/14.007 ≈ 0.0714 meq/mg N) in types/process.rs. Expanded NitrogenCycleOutput to carry alkalinity_consumed_meq for tracing and budget attribution. Wired nitrogen_cycle stage trace notes in engine.rs (total_n_nitrified_mg, alk_consumed_meq). Extended BudgetDelta and BudgetTotals with an alkalinity field so per-system alkalinity attribution is visible in budget tracking and tick-level debug output. Updated water_change budget accounting to track alkalinity exchange. ProcessParams default now references the named constant instead of a magic number.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add named stoichiometric constants to types/process.rs\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"files\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/types/mod.rs\"],\n      \"details\": \"Defined NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 2.0/14.007 and DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 1.0/14.007 with doc comments explaining stoichiometric basis. Changed ProcessParams::default() from magic number 0.1428 to the named constant. Exported both constants through types/mod.rs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Expand NitrogenCycleOutput with alkalinity attribution\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"files\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs\"],\n      \"details\": \"Added alkalinity_consumed_meq field to NitrogenCycleOutput. The value is populated from aob_alk_cost + comammox_alk_cost — NOB does NOT contribute. Added doc comments explaining the stoichiometric basis and that the actual deduction happens inside step_nitrogen_cycle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Wire alkalinity tracing into engine nitrogen_cycle stage\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"files\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs\"],\n      \"details\": \"Changed from discarding the NitrogenCycleOutput to capturing it and emitting stage_trace.note() calls for nitrogen_cycle.total_n_nitrified_mg and nitrogen_cycle.alk_consumed_meq when tracing is enabled.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Extend budget tracking with alkalinity element\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"files\": [\"crates/tank_core/src/types/budget.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/budget_helpers.rs\", \"crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs\"],\n      \"details\": \"Added alkalinity_meq to BudgetTotals (sourced from water.alkalinity_meq_total), alkalinity to BudgetDelta (with serde(default) for backwards compatibility), Element::Alkalinity variant to budget_helpers, and alkalinity tracking in water_change budget accounting. Updated all match arms, debug printing, and assertion helpers to include the new element with meq units.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Create nitrification_alkalinity integration tests\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"files\": [\"crates/tank_core/tests/nitrification_alkalinity.rs\"],\n      \"details\": \"6 tests covering all acceptance criteria: (1) alkalinity_matches_stoichiometry — closed-system mass balance initial_alk - final_alk ≈ NOx_produced × NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N within 15% relative error; (2) cycling_scenario_shows_ph_decline — 24h pre-equilibration then 96h showing pH decline from alkalinity consumption; (3) soft_water_ph_declines_faster_than_hard_water — KH≈2 vs KH≈8 contrast; (4) alkalinity_visible_in_budget_tracking — net alkalinity delta negative and attributed to system:nitrogen_cycle; (5) nob_does_not_consume_additional_alkalinity — NO₂ oxidized but alkalinity unchanged; (6) stoichiometric_constants_match_expected_values — literature values and ProcessParams default consistency.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Run cargo test && cargo clippy && cargo fmt --check\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\",\n      \"files\": [],\n      \"details\": \"All 6 nitrification_alkalinity tests pass. Clippy clean. Fmt clean. Full test suite passes except pre-existing save_load_with_active_cycle_state failure (confirmed unrelated by git stash test).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validation_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Named stoichiometric constants applied once per mg N nitrified (not double-charged at NOB)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 2.0/14.007 defined in types/process.rs. Alkalinity deduction in nitrogen_cycle.rs lines 366-373 only sums aob_alk_cost + comammox_alk_cost. NOB has no alkalinity cost. Test nob_does_not_consume_additional_alkalinity confirms NOB oxidizes nitrite without changing alkalinity (delta < 1e-9 meq).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Cycling scenario without water changes shows pH decline from alkalinity consumption\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Test cycling_scenario_shows_ph_decline: 24h pre-equilibration then 96h of nitrification. Asserts alk_after < alk_before AND ph_after < ph_before AND pH within solver bounds [5.5, 8.5]. Passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Soft-water vs hard-water buffering contrast\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Test soft_water_ph_declines_faster_than_hard_water: KH≈2 (0.71 meq/L) vs KH≈8 (2.86 meq/L) over 72h. Asserts soft water loses larger fraction of alkalinity AND soft water pH drop > hard water pH drop. Passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Closed-system alkalinity mass balance (initial_alk - final_alk ≈ total_N × constant)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Test alkalinity_matches_stoichiometry: 120h, checks (initial_alk - final_alk) vs (NOx_produced × NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N) with <15% relative error. NOx_produced > 0.5 mg N/L × vol ensures significant nitrification occurred. Passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Alkalinity deltas visible in budget tracking and structured tracing\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Test alkalinity_visible_in_budget_tracking: confirms net_delta(Element::Alkalinity) < 0 and system_deltas identifies system:nitrogen_cycle as the consumer. Engine.rs emits stage_trace.note() with nitrogen_cycle.alk_consumed_meq when tracing enabled. BudgetDelta now has alkalinity field tracked in all tick records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Accounting pathway ready for future denitrification (E4b)\",\n      \"evidence\": \"DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 1.0/14.007 defined and exported in types/process.rs with doc comment noting it is reserved for E4b. Test stoichiometric_constants_match_expected_values confirms the constant ≈ 0.0714 and that nitrification/denitrification ratio is exactly 2.0.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Pre-existing save_load_with_active_cycle_state test failure\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"details\": \"This test was failing before this bead's changes (confirmed via git stash). The constant change from 0.1428 to 2.0/14.007 (≈0.14278575) slightly shifts floating-point determinism but is not the root cause. Needs separate investigation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"Budget alkalinity field reuses ElementBudget's in_mg/out_mg naming for meq values\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"details\": \"The alkalinity element reuses the ElementBudget struct whose fields are named in_mg/out_mg even though alkalinity is tracked in meq. A dedicated AlkalinityBudget struct or renaming would be cleaner but was deferred to avoid scope creep. The doc comments clarify the unit mismatch.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"risk\": \"DIC consumption from nitrifier autotrophic growth can mask alkalinity-driven pH decline\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"details\": \"In the full model (not isolated tests), nitrifier growth consumes significant DIC for carbon assimilation. This DIC drop can reduce dissolved CO₂ faster than alkalinity loss drops pH, potentially masking or inverting the expected pH decline. The cycling test required pre-equilibration and relies on default growth yields being modest relative to oxidation rates. Real scenarios with very fast-growing nitrifiers may show counterintuitive pH trajectories.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"281f55bb-040e-4a74-9e08-ad0bc8a8e883","total_cost_usd":7.098432899999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":668,"cache_creation_input_tokens":202273,"cache_read_input_tokens":8391709,"output_tokens":44326,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":202273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2323,"outputTokens":48673,"cacheReadInputTokens":8557982,"cacheCreationInputTokens":202898,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":6.7755434999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":82,"outputTokens":10121,"cacheReadInputTokens":1880749,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67302,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.32288940000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"64d6226d-e014-4534-8db9-058b25f78e76"}
